{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=========================================================================\nHANDOFF — session paused by operator request. READ THIS BLOCK FIRST.\n=========================================================================\n\n## Where things stand\n\nEPIC e369-a449-4773-48fb (adroit-deductible-kakapo) — Jira Server/DC via a Jira-family seam.\nSTATUS: in_progress, claimed by RebarBotNava. Plan review PASSED (pass 8), attestation certified.\n\n8 story children, depth 1, no interior tickets. Dependency order:\n  J1 acb2 -> J2 62d9 -> {J3 aac8, J4 0a94}\n  J5 c97f -> J6 9fd4 (also needs J4)\n  {J3, J6} -> J7 b4e3 -> J8 8c35\n\nTicket-by-ticket:\n  J1 acb2 (newborn-avian-civet)  IN_PROGRESS, claimed. Work COMPLETE, pushed for review.\n       -> Gerrit change 1009: https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1009\n       -> AWAITING LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. CI run 30463387830 was in_progress at pause.\n       -> NOT closeable until Verified +1 lands.\n  J2 62d9  open, unsigned. Description heavily REWRITTEN this session (see below). Cannot be\n       plan-reviewed until J1 CLOSES (review-plan fast-fails INDETERMINATE, no LLM spend).\n  J3 aac8  open, unsigned. Description touched (codec seam alignment). Blocked by J2.\n  J4 0a94  open, unsigned. Untouched. Blocked by J2.\n  J5 c97f  open, PLAN REVIEW PASSED + certified. CLAIMABLE NOW — independent of J1/J2.\n       This is the best parallel work available to the next session.\n  J6 9fd4  open, unsigned. Description edited (TLS/ca_bundle/resolved_statuses ACs). Blocked.\n  J7 b4e3  open, unsigned. Description edited (reciprocal import check, clean-core CI). Blocked.\n  J8 8c35  open, unsigned. Description edited (operator docs). Blocked.\n  fe15 (controlled-ornate-honeybee) NEW BUG filed this session, linked discovered_from J1.\n\n## Environment (recreate exactly)\n\nWorktree: /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family, branch jira-family-seam, based on\norigin/main @ 1bed2f0cd. Its own .venv is provisioned and holds an EDITABLE install of the\nworktree (rebar 0.10.1 -> /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-jira-family/src/rebar), so it runs rebar HEAD.\nALWAYS prefix commands: env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" ...  (the pre-commit hook needs\nruff+mypy on PATH). Gerrit commit-msg hook installed. HEAD = 7fc96b277 (J1's commit).\nGates confirmed ON in rebar.toml: require_plan_review_for_claim, require_plan_review_for_close.\nVerify commands: none pinned per-ticket -> project default make lint && make typecheck && make test\n(the full suite takes ~28 MINUTES: 7471 passed / 37 skipped / 114 deselected).\n\n## Immediate next actions, in order\n\n1. Poll change 1009 for LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1. On Verified -1, open the run; comment\n   'recheck' only if it is a flake. Fix findings with git commit --amend --no-edit (keeps the\n   Change-Id) and re-push.\n2. Submit 1009 once both are green. Then INSIDE the worktree: git fetch origin &&\n   git merge --ff-only origin/main (the close precheck needs the merged rebar-ticket commit\n   reachable from HEAD). NEVER fast-forward the shared main checkout at /Users/joeoakhart/rebar.\n3. Close J1: rebar transition acb2-1823-2f0d-415b in_progress closed.\n4. THEN plan-review J2 (it becomes claimable once J1 closes), claim, and implement.\n5. In parallel at any time: claim J5 c97f (already certified) and build the Docker harness.\n\n## Hard-won lessons — do not relearn these\n\n* COMMIT MESSAGES: write to 50/72 BEFORE the first push. This repo enforces it (commit 514d).\n  I amended after pushing, which ROTATED the Change-Id and orphaned change 1008 (now abandoned).\n* ATTESTATION STALENESS: a plan review PINS its children's material. Editing ANY child after the\n  epic review staleness the epic ('stale-pin-drift') and the claim is refused. Finalize all child\n  text FIRST, review the epic LAST, claim IMMEDIATELY after.\n* PARENT-FIRST CASCADE: claiming a child pulls a still-open parent into progress and runs the\n  PARENT's gate too. J1 could not be claimed until the epic's attestation was fresh.\n* DEPENDENCY ORDER IS ENFORCED: review-plan on a not-yet-claimable ticket fast-fails\n  INDETERMINATE with no LLM spend. The tree is strictly serial; you cannot pre-review children.\n* The plan-review LLM pass takes ~18-22 MINUTES per run. Batch ALL remediations (blocking +\n  worthwhile advisories) into ONE pass rather than one finding per cycle.\n========================================================================="},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785338191288550001,"uuid":"a72c5763-9050-4786-889b-7d2ee1fe1523"}